{#
  The print-ready form of the canonical bilingual report.

  This is the same page, not a second one. KHEPRI-DEC-005 consolidates bilingual
  rendering into one template so that Arabic and English parity has one place to
  be correct; a forked copy would be a second place for it to drift. So this
  template extends `report.html.j2` and fills the two blocks that template left
  empty -- nothing else. Every heading, figure, caveat, citation and disclosure
  on the printed page comes from the parent, unchanged and in the same order.

  Nothing here is marked safe. Font payloads are base64, which uses none of the
  characters HTML escaping touches, so they reach the document byte-identical
  through the same autoescaping environment the web surface renders in. The
  print stylesheet is included as template *source*, exactly as the parent
  includes the screen stylesheet, which is what removes the last reason anyone
  would reach for an exemption.
#}
{% extends "report.html.j2" %}
{% block embedded_fonts %}
<style>
{% for font in fonts %}
@font-face {
  font-family: "{{ font.family }}";
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 400;
  /* `block` rather than `swap`: the payload is already in this document, so
     there is nothing to wait for, and a swap would let a first paint use a
     fallback face that the printed page then captures. */
  font-display: block;
  src: url({{ font.data_uri }}) format("{{ font.font_format }}");
  unicode-range: {{ font.unicode_range }};
}
{% endfor %}
</style>
{% endblock %}
{% block print_stylesheet %}
<style>
{% include print_stylesheet_name %}
</style>
{% endblock %}
